  "name": "Toxoplasma-IgG",
  "code": "TOXIG",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><br></p><table><thead><tr><th><div>Toxoplasma Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>IgG Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgG antibodies indicates past or previous exposure to Toxoplasma gondii. It does not necessarily mean an active infection, as the body develops these antibodies after being exposed to the parasite. Immunity to future infections is usually provided.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>IgM Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgM antibodies suggests a recent or acute infection with Toxoplasma gondii. It indicates an ongoing or recent infection. Additional testing and clinical assessment are necessary to confirm the diagnosis.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Both IgG and IgM Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>Simultaneous presence of both IgG and IgM antibodies suggests an acute infection or reactivation of a previous infection. Further evaluation is required to determine the specific stage and severity of the infection.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Both IgG and IgM Antibodies Negative</div></td><td><div>A negative result for both IgG and IgM antibodies indicates no current or previous exposure to Toxoplasma gondii. However, it does not rule out the possibility of future infections.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
